    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUT_External/job/Texarkana-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor---Education-Leadership_R-097843-3": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor – Education Leadership",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor – Education Leadership Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department CASE- Education (EdD, Curriculum, and Instruction) Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Texarkana invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Educational Leadership. The successful candidate will serve as core faculty in the Doctor of Education (EdD) in Educational Leadership. This position supports doctoral teaching, mentorship, and applied research within a Doctorate of Practice model. The EdD emphasizes systematic inquiry, evidence-based leadership, and organizational improvement across various educational contexts. The program is delivered fully online and includes required synchronous engagement on designated evenings. The standard teaching load is 3/3. Faculty are expected to maintain an active research agenda with peer-reviewed scholarship consistent with tenure and promotion guidelines and aligned with the university’s research priorities. The position includes doctoral mentorship, service to the division and university, and participation in continuous program development. Although remote work is authorized for this position, applicants must be able to periodically attend meetings and other initiatives on campus with prior notice.   Eligibility to work in the U.S. is required at the time of hire. No pre-employment sponsorship is authorized for this position.     ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES:   Teach doctoral-level courses in Educational Leadership within a fully online EdD program, including required synchronous engagement on designated evenings Design and deliver instruction that integrates applied research, organizational improvement, and evidence-based leadership practices Serve on doctoral dissertation committees upon appointment; chair Dissertation of Practice projects following appropriate onboarding Mentor doctoral students through the development, implementation, and dissemination of applied research addressing problems of practice Maintain an active and productive research agenda resulting in peer-reviewed publications consistent with tenure and promotion expectations Present scholarly work at regional, national, or international professional conferences Pursue external funding and grant development opportunities, as appropriate Contribute to program assessment, curriculum refinement, and continuous improvement efforts within the EdD program Support doctoral student recruitment, retention, and completion initiatives Engage in service to the division, university, and profession, including participation in accreditation and institutional effectiveness activities Comply with university policies and institutional standards for graduate education   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Minimum Qualifications Assistant Professor Rank Earned PhD or EdD in Educational Leadership or a closely related field from an accredited institution Demonstrated record of peer-reviewed scholarly publications appropriate to rank Potential for active research agenda in educational leadership or related areas Demonstrated strong evidence of teaching potential Professional experience in educational leadership, administration, or organizational leadership within educational contexts Eligibility to work in the U.S. is required at the time of hire. No pre-employment sponsorship is authorized for this position.  Ability to attend meetings and participate in other initiatives on campus with prior notice   Associate Professor Rank Meet all the minimum requirements listed as Assistant Professor Rank A minimum of 5 years of service at the rank of Assistant Professor Evidence of an active research agenda in educational leadership or related areas Demonstrated effectiveness in graduate-level teaching   Preferred Qualifications Experience serving on or chairing doctoral dissertation committees Record of peer-reviewed publications in reputable journals and evidence of ongoing scholarly productivity Experience teaching graduate-level research methods courses and mentoring doctoral students through the design and implementation of applied research or Dissertation of Practice projects Evidence of or potential for securing external funding and engaging in grant development Experience teaching in fully online graduate programs Experience contributing to program development, accreditation, or institutional effectiveness initiatives   SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL:  This position generally does not supervise employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, transcripts, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu . All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUT_External/job/Texarkana-TX/Lecturer-of-Physics_R-097714": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Physics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Lecturer of Physics Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department CASE - Science & Mathematics Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The non-tenure track faculty position of Lecturer of Physics is responsible for developing, coordinating, and teaching Physics courses in the College of Arts, Sciences, and Education (CASE). The successful candidate will possess documented abilities in teaching and service and will be expected to foster the growth of Physics courses, including building on existing strengths within the College and through collaboration with other faculty across campus. The successful candidate will also address student needs in Physics and assist the Division Chair and Dean in implementing the short- and long-term goals of the College. The anticipated start date for this position is for the Fall of 2027   Eligibility to work in the U.S. is required at the time of hire. No pre-employment sponsorship is authorized for this position.   ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES:   Teach assigned courses (15 credit hours per semester or 30 credit hours per academic year) Work collaboratively with faculty across disciplines Contribute to curriculum and course development Serve on department, college, and university committees, as assigned by the Chair or Dean Serve on professional committees, as approved by the Dean   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Minimum Qualifications A Master’s degree in Physics, or a closely related field with at least 18 semester credit hours in physics at the graduate level by the time of employment Ability to teach various courses within the Physics program Evidence of excellence in teaching Excellent oral/written communication and organizational skills   Preferred Qualifications A Ph.D. in Physics, or closely related field Prior experience teaching physics courses (lectures and labs) at an accredited college or university Experience developing and delivering physics courses online Familiarity with accreditation processes (e.g. SACSCOC, ABET, etc.) and assessment, including data collection, organization, and analysis Excellent interpersonal skills Ability to assist with university and professional service activities, including national and international outreach to, and collaboration with, industry and other academic institutions Lecturers are not assessed for their scholarship; opportunities for research and professional development are often available and encouraged.   Other requirements Ability to travel and work beyond normal office hours Ability to maintain confidentiality SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL: This position does not supervise employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, transcripts, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu . All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
